course: dictionary
lesson: 3753
title: Fluoride and strong teeth
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Fluoride is a natural mineral that helps make teeth strong and protects them from holes, which doctors and dentists call decay. Read the context: «Brush twice a day for about two minutes with fluoride toothpaste, then spit but do not rinse, so the fluoride stays on the teeth.» The words stays on the teeth tell you fluoride works while it sits on your teeth.
explain: Clues also tell you where fluoride is found. «Some places add a small amount of fluoride to tap water to protect teeth.» So it is in toothpaste and sometimes in the water from your tap. The word small matters too: fluoride is used in small amounts.
explain: Try swapping a meaning into the sentence to check it. «Fluoride makes enamel stronger against acid.» If you put strong in place of stronger, the sentence still makes sense, so fluoride must help things become harder to damage.
fact: Fluoride is a natural mineral.
fact: «Fluoride» helps make teeth strong and protects them from decay (holes).
fact: Fluoride is added to most toothpastes and, in many places, to tap water.
fact: Dentists sometimes paint fluoride varnish on children's teeth.
fact: In science, fluoride is a compound of the element fluorine.
exercise: «Toothpaste has fluoride, which makes teeth stronger.» What does fluoride do for teeth? | Makes them taste sweeter | Makes them grow longer | *Makes them stronger and protects them from holes | Turns them into bone
exercise: «Some places add a small amount of fluoride to tap water.» Where else can fluoride be found? | In the air we breathe | In the dentist's chair | *In toothpaste | In sugary snacks
exercise: «Fluoride makes enamel stronger against acid.» Find and copy the word that means the same as strong. | *stronger | enamel | acid | fluoride
test: «Spit the toothpaste out, but do not rinse with lots of water, so a little fluoride stays on the teeth.» Why do we not rinse straight away? | So the toothpaste tastes nicer | So we swallow more fluoride | *So a little fluoride stays on the teeth | Because rinsing makes teeth dirty
test: Which of these is fluoride? | A kind of toothbrush | A sugary snack | A type of tooth | *A natural mineral that helps make teeth strong
exam: «Toothpaste is spat out, not swallowed, because too much swallowed fluoride is not good for the body.» Why should we spit toothpaste out? | Because it tastes bad | Because it makes our breath smell | *Because too much swallowed fluoride is not good for the body | Because we need to save it for later
